            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0449" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-01T15:00:00-00:44">October 1, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>135. Department’s 84, September 30, 5 p.m. I believe it preferable that the
                    proposed interview with President King be put off until I am able to present an
                    acknowledgment of the note quoted in my 133; on this occasion I can explain the
                    Department’s views regarding the necessity of enforcement measures.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reber</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
